NFDH shelf-packing with bounding-box approach: sort pieces by min-height orientation (desc), pack left-to-right row-by-row; try each piece in all 8 orientations to fit current row without increasing height; sweep W from W_min_req to 3*sqrt(T) picking best area. Deliberately NOT using: skyline algorithm, bitmap placement, ILP, or branch-and-bound. Focusing on correctness + fast sweep over widths.
